cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the GQLSA attention mechanism in your research, please cite both the paper and this repository."
title: "GQLSA: Grouped-Query Latent Sparse Attention"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sabid
    given-names: Fardin
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    email: contact.fardinsabid@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/fardinsabid/gqlsa"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22818585"
abstract: >-
  A compositional attention mechanism combining latent KV compression
  (MLA-style), grouped-query head sharing (GQA-style), and content-retrieved
  block sparsity with a fully vectorized random-projection inverted index.
  Linear O(T) attention compute with 4.00x FLOP reduction, 3.68x wall-clock
  speedup, 2.03x memory reduction, and 15.5x KV cache compression vs MHA
  at 4096 tokens on a Tesla T4.
keywords:
  - sparse attention
  - efficient transformers
  - long-context
  - grouped-query attention
  - latent attention
  - large language models
  - attention mechanism
